'''Omega's room''' was a room located in the [[Galactic Empire]]'s [[Tantiss Base]] on the [[planet]] [[Wayland]] where the young [[Cloning|clone]] [[Omega]] lived during her Imperial [[Prisoner|captivity]] during or after [[18 BBY]]. A small, barren space, Omega lived in the room for around 164 [[Standard day|days]] while she was made to be a medical assistant to [[Doctor]]s [[Nala Se]] and [[Emerie Karr]]. Omega ultimately [[Escape from Tantiss|escaped]] from Tantiss Base, leaving the room behind.

==Description==
{{Quote|How are you feeling?''"<br />"''Like a prisoner.|Emerie Karr greets Omega in her room|<ref name="Confined" />}}
[[File:Confined-TBBS3-Thumbnail.png|thumb|left|250px|Omega gazing out the window of her room.]]
Omega's room<ref name="Databank">{{Databank|omega-s-room-mount-tantiss|Omega's room (Mount Tantiss)}}</ref> was located within the [[Galactic Empire]]'s [[Tantiss Base]] at [[Mount Tantiss]] on the [[planet]] [[Wayland]]. Following her [[Capture of Omega|capture]] on<ref name="Confined" /> the planet<ref name="Ord Mantell">{{Databank|ord-mantell|Ord Mantell}}</ref> [[Ord Mantell]]<ref name="Confined" /> during or after [[18 BBY]],<ref name="Date">{{TBBDate|216}}</ref> the young [[Cloning|clone]] [[Omega]] was [[Prisoner|imprisoned]] in Tantiss Base, with the room serving as her personal quarters. The small room had a single entrance, with an interior doorway having an elevated step. The room had a bed positioned on the far wall near the door, a sink that consistently dripped [[water]] from its faucet, and a small, barred [[Viewport|window]] above the side of the bed that overlooked the [[jungle]] and [[mountain]]s that lay beyond the base. It was bare of possessions save for a [[Color|gray]] lunch pail, which Omega kept under her bed, and a [[straw tooka]] she made with material taken from the [[lurca hound]] [[Lurca kennels|kennels]], which she kept hidden, as personal effects were not allowed.<ref name="Confined" />

==History==
{{Quote|Take her back to her room and restrict her access.|Royce Hemlock orders Emerie Karr to return Omega to her room|<ref name="Confined" />}}
[[File:Omega-Gets-Her-Straw-Tooka-Back.png|thumb|right|300px|Omega notices her straw tooka has been returned.]]
Omega lived in the room for around 164 [[Standard day|days]]<ref name="Confined Ep Guide">{{SW|url=series/the-bad-batch/confined-episode-guide|text="Confined" Episode Guide &#124; The Bad Batch}}</ref> while she was made to assist both [[Doctor]] [[Emerie Karr]] and the [[Kaminoan]] and fellow prisoner [[Nala Se]] in the Empire's [[Project Necromancer|medical experiments]], making a mark for each day on the side of the window sill. Her straw [[tooka doll]] was confiscated when Karr and a pair of [[clone commando]]s entered the room for an inspection. A short [[time]] later, Doctor [[Royce Hemlock]] confined Omega to her room following her releasing the [[lurca hound]] designated LH-201, who she had named [[Batcher]], and threatened to hurt [[Crosshair]], a fellow clone prisoner and former member of Omega's [[squad]], as a means to keep Omega in line. That night, as Omega sulked in her room, Karr left the straw [[tooka]] in the room for Omega to show her sympathy.<ref name="Confined" /> 

During Omega and Crosshair's attempt to [[Escape from Tantiss|escape]] the base, Karr caught them and tried to convince Omega to return to her room, but Omega refused, and Crosshair eventually [[stun]]ned the doctor. Omega's escape plan was successful,<ref name="Shadows" /> as she and Crosshair reunited with their squad, [[Clone Force 99]], leaving her room behind.<ref name="Different">{{TBB|A Different Approach}}</ref> She and the rest of Clone Force 99 later [[Skirmish on Wayland|returned]] to free the other prisoners from Tantiss Base, partially destroying the facility and leading to its decommission.<ref name="Cavalry">{{TBB|The Cavalry Has Arrived}}</ref>

==Behind the scenes==
Omega's room first appeared in "[[Confined]],"<ref name="Confined" /> the first episode of [[The Bad Batch Season 3|Season 3]] of ''[[Star Wars: The Bad Batch]]'', released on [[February 21]], [[2024]].<ref name="Air date">{{SW|url=news/the-bad-batch-season-3-trailer|text=Watch the ''Star Wars: The Bad Batch'' Season 3 Trailer}}</ref> After first being pictured in the Season 3 trailer on [[January 22]], 2024,<ref name="Trailer">{{SWYouTube|Oa5zeHdSwdQ|The Bad Batch &#124; The Final Season Official Trailer &#124; Disney+|sw_url=video/the-bad-batch-the-final-season-official-trailer-disney}}</ref> Omega's room was later identified in its [[Databank (2014-)|Databank]] entry published on [[StarWars.com]].<ref name="Databank" /> While the "room" in the name was originally capitalized,<ref name="Databank Old">{{Databank|omega-s-room-mount-tantiss|Omega's Room (Mount Tantiss)|oldversion=20240301085737}}</ref> by [[June 23]], 2024, the Databank had been updated to have the "room" in lowercase.<ref name="Databank" />

